{"@id": "_:b317httpc0liddOtlocdOtgovresourcesworks22953559", "@type": ["http://id.loc.gov/ontologies/bibframe/Summary"], "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [{"@value": "\"Invented stand-in for publisher copy. A new manager learns to run a team of engineers. The book walks through the first weeks, the one-to-ones and the hiring rounds. What does \"done\" mean when nobody writes code any more? It answers that, and then some. Every chapter ends with a short list of things to try on Monday morning, so the advice does not stay on the page. Later parts widen the view to the whole department: how teams talk to each other, how careers grow on two ladders, and how remote work changes the daily routine. The last chapter looks ahead to the next role.\" -- Publisher description."}]},
